From: SKJ Wine
Subject: websocket: implement the client side of the WebSocket Protocol Component API

websocket.dll only created handles; everything else was a stub. .NET Framework's
ClientWebSocket runs on this API (WebSocketProtocolComponent): its static constructor already
calls WebSocketBeginClientHandshake, so any WebSocket use failed with a TypeInitializationException.
Medal's recorder talks to Medal this way.

Implemented: client handles (with the caller's buffer block, as .NET passes it), client
handshake headers and Sec-WebSocket-Accept check, send queue (framing, masking, fragmentation
into the send area), receive queue (frame parsing, fragments larger than the receive area,
close and pong indication, automatic pong for pings), global properties. Server side stays a stub.

